> **Farzana's take:** White gold is where the asscher shows itself most clearly. There is no warm metal tone softening the geometry. No copper-rose creating romantic contrast. It is just the diamond and the step-cut, in a cold white frame. That means white gold asscher rings are the most unforgiving — the stone has to be right. VS1. E or F color. But when you get it right, there is nothing more architectural or precise in engagement ring design. It is the asscher at its purest.

