## Lab Asscher Diamonds for White Gold Settings

Lab-grown asscher diamonds follow the same D-F color rule in white metal. The Color Amplifier effect applies equally — the cold white baseline makes any warmth in the stone more visible, regardless of whether the stone is natural or lab-grown.

In white gold, D-color lab stones make more strategic sense than in yellow or rose gold. The color distinction between D and E is more visible in white metal. If you are buying lab to maximize size, D-color remains a smart choice — you are not paying a D premium that disappears in the metal.

